  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing WASH Services in the Rohingya Response (Ukhia)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to improve and sustain the public health of 65,430 refugees (directly in camps 3 and 4, and through technical support to other United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR) camps in Ukhia) through the delivery of inclusive, sustainable and good quality Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) services.   As the refugee influx crisis enters into its 4th year, the focus of this project and Oxfam&apos;s WASH strategy is to consolidate and sustain gains and improvement achieved through the last three years, and provide technical and strategic inputs to address sustainable WASH service provisions and most appropriate operation and maintenance approaches based on previous learning and practice.</narrative>
  </description>
